{"duration_api_ms":81244,"stop_reason":"tool_use","session_id":"5f6d8281-eb9c-4899-921d-13b4de749122","total_cost_usd":0.5187350000000001,"usage":{"input_tokens":4,"cache_creation_input_tokens":90936,"cache_read_input_tokens":94185,"output_tokens":7392,"output_tokens_details":{"thinking_tokens":3052},"server_tool_use":{"web_search_requests":0,"web_fetch_requests":0},"service_tier":"standard","cache_creation":{"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":90936,"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0},"inference_geo":"not_available","iterations":[{"input_tokens":2,"output_tokens":2144,"cache_read_input_tokens":89863,"cache_creation_input_tokens":5395,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":5395},"type":"message"}],"speed":"standard"},"modelUsage":{"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001":{"inputTokens":62131,"outputTokens":19,"cacheReadInputTokens":0,"cacheCreationInputTokens":0,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.062226,"contextWindow":200000,"maxOutputTokens":32000,"thinkingTokens":0,"canonicalModel":"claude-haiku-4-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"},"claude-sonnet-5":{"inputTokens":4,"outputTokens":7392,"cacheReadInputTokens":94185,"cacheCreationInputTokens":90936,"webSearchRequests":0,"costUSD":0.45650900000000005,"contextWindow":1000000,"maxOutputTokens":64000,"thinkingTokens":3052,"canonicalModel":"claude-sonnet-5","provider":"firstParty","costBasis":"list"}},"permission_denials":[],"terminal_reason":"completed","fast_mode_state":"off","fast_mode_disabled_reason":"sdk_opt_in_required","subagent_stats":{"spawned":0,"requested":{"background":0,"foreground":0,"unset":0},"started_in_background":0,"max_depth":0,"spawned_by_subagents":0,"completed":0,"failed":0,"killed":{"parent":0,"user":0,"system":0},"refused":{"depth_limit":0,"concurrency_limit":0,"budget":0},"by_type":{}},"is_error":false,"num_turns":3,"subtype":"success","api_error_status":null,"result":"{\"requirements\":[{\"id\":\"req-1-service-on-node4\",\"requirement\":\"node4 runs a persistent HTTP service on TCP port 8080\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A systemd-managed python3 http.server was started and enabled on node4:8080, verified active and answering locally and remotely before and after the node4 restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-44684709bd734ac5\",\"cmd-fe39d1c476c24a0c\",\"cmd-98e114296f6d4f36\",\"cmd-a87cfe93d74241cd\"]},{\"id\":\"req-2-publish-on-node2-transit-80\",\"requirement\":\"Service is published on TCP port 80 of node2's transit address\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"A DNAT/port-forward (pf rdr) rule on node2 maps transit interface tcp/80 to 10.10.14.2:8080, with a matching pass rule; curls to http://10.10.12.2:80/ from node1 and node3 return node4's content both before and after node2's restart.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-0da78c2e97fc47fd\",\"cmd-5baec3db64784985\",\"cmd-c0283ea986294ae4\",\"cmd-9466acae6a3c4906\",\"cmd-65e7785865f548fc\",\"cmd-31b975c4dedf40ff\",\"cmd-5016f8496736493d\",\"cmd-f56ab276813d4398\"]},{\"id\":\"req-3-node1-route-to-node2-transit\",\"requirement\":\"node1 has a route to node2's transit address\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node1's eth1 is configured (persistently, via VyOS configure/commit/save) with 10.10.12.1/24, directly connected to node2's transit address 10.10.12.2, and the successful curl through node1's forwarding path confirms reachability; ip_forward is enabled.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-2ee69bdbfc16497b\",\"cmd-b26c301b9f984abb\",\"cmd-f5de10df7639430d\",\"cmd-65e7785865f548fc\"]},{\"id\":\"req-4-node3-reaches-via-node2-not-node4\",\"requirement\":\"node3 on lan-a reaches the service by asking node2 rather than addressing node4 directly\",\"status\":\"satisfied\",\"summary\":\"node3 was given a persistent route to 10.10.12.0/24 via node1; curl to node2's transit address (10.10.12.2:80) succeeds and returns node4's content repeatedly, including after all four restarts, while a direct curl attempt to node4 (10.10.14.2:8080) times out because node3 has no route to lan-b and falls back to the unrelated control-plane default route.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-91b8bdd76e1140b4\",\"cmd-31b975c4dedf40ff\",\"cmd-7b1da98bc6994be7\",\"cmd-97c4bd2c47514a65\",\"cmd-700e7eaf5f474353\",\"cmd-f56ab276813d4398\"]}],\"confidence\":0.9,\"operational_hygiene\":{\"score\":0.8,\"summary\":\"Most state-changing commands map directly to legitimate prerequisites (interface addressing, DNAT/route configuration, service creation) or to bounded final evidence collection. Several exploratory mutations occurred during initial topology discovery: node1's eth1 was temporarily flushed and reassigned to the wrong subnet (10.10.14.1) while probing physical adjacency, then flushed back to the correct 10.10.12.1/24 (cmd-6bd4b607c25a4685, cmd-c6f27d0e15ad4d31, reverted by cmd-8e2e5f71ecbf431c); node2's vtnet1/vtnet2 addresses were likewise swapped and swapped back during the same probing (cmd-9e5d3ab7718a4b45, corrected by cmd-b021b18c0ceb4d17). Temporary 'antrieb: temp allow icmp for topology probe' pf rules were added to node2 during discovery (visible in cmd-432588fc2eaa4247) and confirmed absent from the final restored configuration (cmd-6470a5964ec54904 shows zero 'antrieb'-labeled rules), indicating they were cleaned up. All of these were bounded, low-risk, and left no residue in the final state. No unnecessary destructive actions, abandoned files, or exposed insecure configuration were observed in the after-executor snapshot.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-6bd4b607c25a4685\",\"cmd-c6f27d0e15ad4d31\",\"cmd-8e2e5f71ecbf431c\",\"cmd-9e5d3ab7718a4b45\",\"cmd-b021b18c0ceb4d17\",\"cmd-432588fc2eaa4247\",\"cmd-6470a5964ec54904\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"All material outcomes of the task are directly satisfied: node4's HTTP service is published via a DNAT rule on node2's transit address at port 80, node1 has a direct route/adjacency to that address with forwarding enabled, and node3 was demonstrated (via curl and a failed direct attempt to node4) to reach the service only by addressing node2. The executor additionally ran the full node-restart evidence protocol on all four nodes, capturing pre-restart healthy baselines, reboot acknowledgements, changed boot identities, and post-restart recovery of addressing, routes, NAT rules, and the working end-to-end curl path for each node — this is not a task requirement but strengthens confidence in the persistence of the solution.\",\"limitations\":[\"The claim that node1 has 'a route' to node2's transit address rests on the two being directly connected on the same /24 rather than an explicit static route entry; this is an equally valid competent implementation given the topology, not a gap.\",\"Some intermediate diagnostic mutations (interface address swaps, temporary ICMP pass rules) were not individually traced end-to-end for removal beyond the final grep-based check on node2; the after-executor lifecycle snapshot corroborates no residual artifacts but does not exhaustively enumerate every intermediate pf rule.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1-service-on-node4","requirement":"node4 runs a persistent HTTP service on TCP port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"A systemd-managed python3 http.server was started and enabled on node4:8080, verified active and answering locally and remotely before and after the node4 restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-44684709bd734ac5","cmd-fe39d1c476c24a0c","cmd-98e114296f6d4f36","cmd-a87cfe93d74241cd"]},{"id":"req-2-publish-on-node2-transit-80","requirement":"Service is published on TCP port 80 of node2's transit address","status":"satisfied","summary":"A DNAT/port-forward (pf rdr) rule on node2 maps transit interface tcp/80 to 10.10.14.2:8080, with a matching pass rule; curls to http://10.10.12.2:80/ from node1 and node3 return node4's content both before and after node2's restart.","evidence_ids":["cmd-0da78c2e97fc47fd","cmd-5baec3db64784985","cmd-c0283ea986294ae4","cmd-9466acae6a3c4906","cmd-65e7785865f548fc","cmd-31b975c4dedf40ff","cmd-5016f8